  <heading>STLRO</heading>
  <desc>
    <brief>
      <para>Store-release octaword</para>
    </brief>
    <authored>
      <para>This instruction stores a 32-byte (octaword) vector register to a memory address
generated by a 64-bit scalar base, plus an immediate offset.
The base register must be aligned to 32 bytes if alignment is checked.</para>
      <para>This instruction is unpredicated.</para>
      <para>The instruction has memory ordering semantics as described in
<xref linkend="BEIHCHEF">Load-Acquire, Store-Release</xref>.</para>
      <para>This instruction requires that the Effective SVE vector length is at least 256 bits.</para>
      <para>This instruction is illegal when executed in Streaming SVE mode, unless FEAT_SME_FA64 is implemented and enabled.</para>
    </authored>
    <uses_dit condition="FEAT_SVE2 is implemented or FEAT_SME is implemented">True</uses_dit>
    <sm_policy>SM_0_only</sm_policy>
    <is_store>True</is_store>
  </desc>
  <operationalnotes>
    <operationalnote>
      <operationalnote_content>
        <para>This instruction is a data-independent-time instruction as described in <xref linkend="BEICCDDAB3">About PSTATE.DIT</xref>.</para>
      </operationalnote_content>
    </operationalnote>
  </operationalnotes>
